From 4771b8161c843831cb8a24fa95865528f41b5fcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shkosugi <sin.kosugi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:47:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] Type resolution: a missing assembly is null, not an
 exception, as on .NET Framework

Type.GetType(name, assemblyResolver, typeResolver, throwOnError) lets an exception
from the assembly resolver through, whatever throwOnError says. The resolvers here
called AssemblyLoadContext.LoadFromAssemblyName, which throws FileNotFoundException
for an assembly that is not there: BuildManager.GetType(type, throwOnError: false)
threw where .NET Framework returns null (DNN's ProviderInstaller: providers named in
web.config and installed later, DNNConnect.CKEditorProvider). The resolvers return
null for it, as the ones that already caught it do; with throwOnError, Type.GetType
throws FileNotFoundException itself.
